    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass and all public exports are intact. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n**1. Missing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` export (finetune/governance.test.js)**\n- Added named export of `APPROVAL_STATUSES` and other constants from `finetune/index.js`\n- The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export\n\n**2. Incorrect `toxicityMetric` signature (eval/index.test.js)**\n- Changed `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs)`\n- The function was receiving `references` as the second parameter (passed by `runEvaluations`), which were being treated as banned terms, causing innocent words to be flagged as toxic\n- Now the metric consistently takes only the outputs parameter, matching the calling convention used by the other metrics\n\nBoth fixes maintain backward compatibility and preserve all public exports. All 28 tests now pass across all 8 test files.",
